WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:11.850
When I was ten, my future looked so clear to
me.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.770
Married to Josh Hartnett with two kids.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.930
Driving a Honda Odyssey.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.600
Not a bad life.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.360
Got another one coming.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.790
Push! What's going on?

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:31.850
There's been a mistake. I came here to see
one of my friends. He had a heart attack.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.790
Don't worry. You did great with the first
two. Just keep pushing. You're having

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:36.570
triplets.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.700
I'm- triplets?

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:40.320
And now...

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.830
baby three.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.660
But here's the thing about childhood
fantasies. They almost never come true.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.830
Congratulations. It's a podcast.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:58.050
Mabel. Mabel!

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.190
Mabel.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.060
The doctor said I can finally go home.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:03.070
What?

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.220
Yeah. No no no no no. The man had a full on
heart attack five days ago. You rush him in

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.220
here, stick in a stent to prop up his creaky
arteries.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.150
Nobody said creaky.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.900
Now you're just going to go and send him off
into the world.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:19.410
Mabel, I need to get back. My show opens in
two days and my star is about to be charged

00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.340
with murder.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:20.550
Doctor, maybe

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.800
you should just run a few more tests to be
sure.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.000
His body responded very well to the stent,
although I'm sure it was quite a scare for

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:27.840
all of you.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.550
I wasn't scared.

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:33.420
Oh, is that so? You know, I was just
pretending to be unconscious when I heard you

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.850
wailing. I can't let him go.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.940
Come back to me, you sweet son of a bitch.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.630
I was doing a performance for the nurses. They're big fans
of mine. What am I going to do? Not be

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:43.860
Charles Hayden Savage?

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.930
Oh, admit it, you're obsessed with me.

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:51.150
I can't believe I actually missed this. Come
on, Putnam, we've got work to do.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.410
Yes! Let's go. Yes, yes.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:59.250
For starters, if Loretta made up her
confession to protect her son, don't we need

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.850
to prove that her son is Ben's real killer to
get her out?

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.750
Loretta's been in jail a few days now. I
wonder if she's shaved her head and gotten

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:07.860
all jagged.

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:11.490
I can't let her take the fall for this. She's
the love of my life.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.040
Love? I thought you were just hooking up.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.080
Oh, we hooked up.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:18.450
We hooked up big time.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:22.500
We hooked up and down and every which
direction. You name a.-

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.490
I promise we will get her home to you.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.950
No matter how many face tattoos she has now.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:33.420
Charles, did you learn anything from those
police interrogations we so skillfully

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.020
recorded?

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.130
Actually, we haven't watched them yet. We
were sitting by your bedside this whole time.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.850
Mabel wanted to wait so you could be a part
of it. Little softie.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.500
No, I didn't, it wasn't like I was like,
let's hold hands and watch it together. It

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.570
was just like. Shut up.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:55.930
Okay. We're focusing on Dickie. Loretta
clearly thinks that he's guilty. That's why

00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:00.850
she confessed to protect him. Ben was
poisoned and then later pushed down the

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:07.000
elevator shaft. But we don't know whose hanky
he was holding on to when he died. I mean, it

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.410
could be Dickie's.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:13.360
We know that someone wrote Fucking Pig in
lipstick on his mirror, and we have footage

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:17.920
of him in a heated moment talking to an
unseen person, possibly a lover.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:24.280
Can we just take a beat to appreciate how
magical this is? The three of us reunited at

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:30.370
last, investigating as one. Mabel, you stayed
faithful to the podcast. You should take the

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:33.400
lead. Just the besties are back.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.540
Oh, that should be our opening line.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.280
You just said Mabel should take the lead.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:42.040
Can I make a suggestion? I narrowly escaped
death. And now you won't let me live.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.300
Wah wah wah wah wah wah.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.140
This is fucking weird.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:48.430
Okay, okay.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:50.980
The besties are back.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.990
The besties are back.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:02.370
It may take two to tango, but it takes three
to solve a murder of an ill fated movie star.

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:07.430
Welcome to a brand new episode of Only
Murders in the Building.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:08.250
Perfection.

